WEBVTT

00:00:00.469 --> 00:00:05.165
Welcome to Alaventra. Rank in
search. Get recommended by AI.

00:00:06.164 --> 00:00:12.014
In tutorial 7.11, you'll see which of
your pages Google left out of search, why,

00:00:12.064 --> 00:00:13.612
and what to do about each one.

00:00:14.643 --> 00:00:19.093
First, open Indexing. Every day
we check your pages with Google.

00:00:19.143 --> 00:00:23.118
The summary shows how many are in
Google search, how many need you,

00:00:23.168 --> 00:00:24.602
and any that dropped out.

00:00:25.605 --> 00:00:29.630
New pages lists what you wrote
or added in the last thirty days.

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:33.497
Google usually needs a few weeks
for those, so they just need time.

00:00:34.502 --> 00:00:38.077
Existing pages groups every
other page by its reason.

00:00:38.127 --> 00:00:41.677
Each group says what it means,
what we do, and what you do.

00:00:42.626 --> 00:00:47.351
Click Details and history to see what
Google says, what our own visit found,

00:00:47.401 --> 00:00:49.484
and how the page changed over time.

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:55.450
Some fixes only you can make on your
website, like removing a noindex instruction,

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:59.104
or a page that is not
found. Click Open the step.

00:01:00.139 --> 00:01:04.169
Steps on your website lists the
pages. Copy them, make the change,

00:01:04.219 --> 00:01:07.886
then click I've done it, check now.
Show me how walks you through it.

00:01:09.093 --> 00:01:12.118
When Google knows a page
but has not read it yet,

00:01:12.168 --> 00:01:15.909
we suggest pages of yours already
in search that should link to it.

00:01:17.093 --> 00:01:21.218
When Google read a page and left
it out, click Improve this page.

00:01:21.268 --> 00:01:26.021
Write a page opens with that page filled
in, and nothing starts until you run it.

00:01:27.016 --> 00:01:31.891
Once we see your fix, the page moves to
Fixed on your site, waiting for Google.

00:01:31.941 --> 00:01:34.426
Google decides when it
reads the page again.

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:39.355
For a few important pages, you
can ask Google to read them again.

00:01:39.405 --> 00:01:43.458
You do that yourself in Search Console.
Show me how gives you the steps.

00:01:44.489 --> 00:01:49.079
Archives and search pages are left
out on purpose, and that's fine.

00:01:49.129 --> 00:01:52.710
Dropped out lists pages that were
in search and are not any more.

00:01:53.674 --> 00:01:56.324
Google updates lists
what Google announced.

00:01:56.374 --> 00:02:01.621
After an update finishes, you see which of
your pages lost ground, held, or gained.

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:05.950
While an update is rolling
out, pages move around,

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:09.686
so we hold back suggestions to
rewrite pages until it's over.

00:02:10.723 --> 00:02:13.048
Finally, Indexing is free.

00:02:13.098 --> 00:02:16.548
Click Change to switch it on or
off in Tracking and monitors,

00:02:16.598 --> 00:02:19.647
and choose how many pages are
checked with Google a day.

00:02:20.667 --> 00:02:25.067
So, open Indexing, read each
group, fix what's on your website,

00:02:25.117 --> 00:02:29.162
help Google find or improve a
page, ask Google to read it again,

00:02:29.212 --> 00:02:30.966
and follow Google's updates.

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:36.935
You know where every page stands. Next,
check if AI assistants name your business,

00:02:36.985 --> 00:02:38.879
in tutorial 8.1.
